# The floor's scenery, drawn by hand, one character per pixel.
#
# This is the source. `build-tiles.py` derives site/assets/floor/tiles.png and its
# index; never edit those. Every tile is 16 by 16 and every row is exactly 16
# characters — the builder refuses anything else rather than silently padding.
#
# One palette, fixed, and it does not follow the reader's theme (ADR-0013). A sage
# carpet, cream walls, warm wood: an office interior with its own light.

palette
. none
c #5f7269
C #6b7f74
v #51625a
f #857f70
F #918b7b
W #e0dacb
w #cdc5b2
s #a99f8a
n #6e6455
e #6b4630
D #a9764a
d #c99a63
l #e0bb85
L #f0ece2
M #22282f
m #39424b
b #3f6f88
B #9fd0e0
a #8b939b
A #c2c9cf
r #6e3644
R #96505f
g #3f6b3c
G #5d8f4f
t #a6603f
z #3c5a6b
Z #8fb6cc
o #a8763e
k #1c1c20
end

# Carpet tile with the seam on two edges and a small woven diamond at the centre.
# Laid across the whole plate it is what stops a large area from reading as a fill.
tile carpet
vvvvvvvvvvvvvvvv
vccccccccccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
vcccccccCccccccc
vccccccCCCcccccc
vcccccCCCCCccccc
vccccCCCCCCCcccc
vcccccCCCCCccccc
vccccccCCCcccccc
vcccccccCccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
vccccccccccccccc
end

